#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:17
msgid "rosbag2: Overriding Quality of Service (QoS) Policies - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:20
msgid ""
"Quality of Service (QoS) compatibility can affect whether Ros2Bag records or "
"plays back data from ROS topics correctly. This article shows how to "
"override Ros2Bag QoS profile settings with a YAML file. After you follow "
"these steps, you can apply topic-specific QoS policies for recording and "
"playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:28
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Override Ros2Bag QoS profile settings for recording and playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:33
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:36
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:38
msgid ""
"With the introduction of DDS in ROS 2, Quality of Service (QoS) "
"compatibility for publisher/subscriber nodes needs to be considered when "
"recording and playing back data. More detail on how QoS works can be found :"
"doc:`here <../../../ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-"
"Settings>`. For the purposes of this guide, it is sufficient to know that "
"only the reliability and durability policies affect whether publishers/"
"subscribers are compatible and can receive data from one other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:42
msgid ""
"Ros2Bag adapts its requested/offered QoS profile when recording/playing data "
"from a topic to prevent dropped messages. During playback, Ros2bag also "
"attempts to preserve the policy originally offered by the topic. Certain "
"situations may require specifying explicit QoS profile settings so Ros2Bag "
"can record/playback topics. These QoS profile overrides can be specified via "
"the CLI using the ``--qos-profile-overrides-path`` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:48
msgid "Using QoS Overrides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:50
msgid ""
"The YAML schema for the profile overrides is a dictionary of topic names "
"with key/value pairs for each QoS policy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:52
msgid ""
"topic_name: str\n"
"  qos_policy_name: str\n"
"  ...\n"
"  qos_duration: object\n"
"    sec: int\n"
"    nsec: int"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:61
msgid ""
"If a policy value is not specified, the value will fallback to the default "
"used by Ros2Bag. If you specify a Duration based policy such as ``deadline`` "
"or ``lifespan``, you will need to specify both seconds and nanoseconds. "
"Policy values are determined by the policy's short keys which can be found "
"using ``ros2topic`` verbs such as ``ros2 topic pub --help``. All values are "
"replicated below for reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:66
msgid ""
"history: [keep_all, keep_last]\n"
"depth: int\n"
"reliability: [system_default, reliable, best_effort, unknown]\n"
"durability: [system_default, transient_local, volatile, unknown]\n"
"deadline:\n"
"  sec: int\n"
"  nsec: int\n"
"lifespan:\n"
"  sec: int\n"
"  nsec: int\n"
"liveliness: [system_default, automatic, manual_by_topic, unknown]\n"
"liveliness_lease_duration:\n"
"  sec: int\n"
"  nsec: int\n"
"avoid_ros_namespace_conventions: [true, false]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:85
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:87
msgid ""
"Consider a topic ``/talker`` offering a ``transient_local`` Durability "
"policy. ROS 2 publishers by default request ``volatile`` Durability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:90
msgid ""
"$ ros2 topic pub -r 0.1 --qos-durability transient_local /talker std_msgs/"
"String \"data: Hello World\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:94
msgid ""
"In order for Ros2Bag to record the data, we would want to override the "
"recording policy for that specific topic like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:96
msgid ""
"# durability_override.yaml\n"
"/talker:\n"
"  durability: transient_local\n"
"  history: keep_all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:103
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:118
msgid "And call it from the CLI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:105
msgid ""
"$ ros2 bag record -a -o my_bag --qos-profile-overrides-path "
"durability_override.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:109
msgid ""
"If we want to playback the bag file but with a different Reliability policy, "
"we can specify one as such;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:111
msgid ""
"# reliability_override.yaml\n"
"/talker:\n"
"  reliability: best_effort\n"
"  history: keep_all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:120
msgid ""
"$ ros2 bag play --qos-profile-overrides-path reliability_override.yaml my_bag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:124
msgid "We can see the results with ``ros2 topic``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback.rst:126
msgid "$ ros2 topic echo --qos-reliability best_effort /talker std_msgs/String"
msgstr ""
